meta {
  name: 1. Dev Top Up (A)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/dev/wallet-topup
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Telegram-Init-Data: {{initData}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "amount_toman": 1000000
  }
}

docs {
  Credits User A's own wallet with a made-up amount — no real payment
  involved. Only reachable when the server is running with
  ENABLE_DEV_TOOLS=true AND the request comes from localhost (see
  app/dev/router.py) — you'll get a 404 otherwise, on purpose.

  This is currently the ONLY way to get wallet balance for manual
  testing: real Telegram Stars payment and manual card-to-card top-up
  are both phase 2 (see TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENTS.md section 10).

  1,000,000 Toman covers a 10-star offer (the "1. Create Offer" default)
  many times over, at the default rate of 4,000 Toman/Star.
}
